	(text "NIBBLE CARD MEMCTL - DATA MEMORY CONTROL: the address register and the write and read gates for the slot cards"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "01689ffb-cf69-466a-b915-8e14e40f14a4")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  57 transistors, 38 resistors, 4 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: BUS3#..BUS0# (an address while MAI), MAI, MI, MO, CLK.\nTo the slot cards over the LINK ribbon (2x6, chained along the eight slot cards): MAR3..0 and their complements, MIN (low = write allowed: MI and MPH), MON (low = read: MO).\nMAR is four transparent latches open while MAI and MPH (the address rides the bus for the whole tick).  MPH is a pulse in the middle of the tick, from the falling edge of CLK until\nCLKD (CLK through 100k into 2.2 nF) decays past a threshold, 60 to 350 us: the address latch closes and the write ends far from both clock edges (D054: gated by PH1, the low half of CLK,\nthey ended at the rising edge, where the next tick's data reached the bus before this card saw the edge).  Each slot card selects its pair of slots from MAR3..1 with jumpers and its even/odd slot with MAR0."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a3b799fb-04ad-4899-9e5a-7319e3e7e0e7")
	)
	(text "MID-TICK PULSE (D054): CLKD is CLK through 100k into 2.2 nF (drawn on the sheet); MPH = NOR(CLK, NOT CLKD) is high from the falling edge of CLK until CLKD decays past a threshold, 60 to 350 us: the address latch closes and the write ends in the middle of the tick, far from both edges"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5b993d4f-a322-422b-b549-76edb5c092c5")
	)
